1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,339
Every Friday, Laddoo
Lab sells out by noon.

2
00:00:03,639 --> 00:00:06,207
But every Monday, packs come back unsold.

3
00:00:06,757 --> 00:00:08,589
The answers were there all along.

4
00:00:08,589 --> 00:00:10,493
They were just scattered everywhere.

5
00:00:11,143 --> 00:00:12,683
Laddoo Lab is growing.

6
00:00:12,683 --> 00:00:16,469
Zoya now sells to her neighbours
and her college every week.

7
00:00:16,819 --> 00:00:19,262
Arjun writes every sale in a notebook.

8
00:00:19,613 --> 00:00:22,435
Dev reads customer messages on his phone.

9
00:00:22,785 --> 00:00:25,037
And Nani remembers who liked what.

10
00:00:25,037 --> 00:00:27,192
But nobody puts it all together.

11
00:00:27,842 --> 00:00:30,737
So what is a marketing information system?

12
00:00:31,037 --> 00:00:34,731
Philip Kotler wrote about the
idea in nineteen sixty six.

13
00:00:34,731 --> 00:00:37,757
He called it the firm's
marketing nerve center.

14
00:00:38,107 --> 00:00:43,204
His textbook calls it people, equipment
and procedures, that gather, sort,

15
00:00:43,204 --> 00:00:47,918
analyze, evaluate and share needed,
timely and accurate information with

16
00:00:47,918 --> 00:00:49,752
marketing decision makers.

17
00:00:50,102 --> 00:00:54,533
In simple words: the right facts, to
the right person, in time to decide.

18
00:00:55,183 --> 00:00:57,395
Let's watch Laddoo Lab build one.

19
00:00:57,745 --> 00:00:59,211
Step one, gather.

20
00:00:59,211 --> 00:01:03,736
Arjun's notebook, Dev's messages
and Nani's notes go into one sheet.

21
00:01:04,086 --> 00:01:05,259
Step two, sort.

22
00:01:05,259 --> 00:01:08,099
Every sale gets a day,
a place and a buyer.

23
00:01:08,449 --> 00:01:09,955
Step three, analyze.

24
00:01:09,955 --> 00:01:12,181
A simple chart shows the pattern.

25
00:01:12,531 --> 00:01:15,140
On Fridays, people want forty packs.

26
00:01:15,140 --> 00:01:17,053
On Mondays, only fifteen.

27
00:01:17,403 --> 00:01:18,698
Step four, share.

28
00:01:18,698 --> 00:01:21,212
Zoya sends the chart to the whole team.

29
00:01:21,562 --> 00:01:22,895
Step five, decide.

30
00:01:22,895 --> 00:01:25,960
Nani makes more for Friday,
and less for Monday.

31
00:01:26,310 --> 00:01:29,676
Unsold packs fall from
twenty a week to just four.

32
00:01:29,676 --> 00:01:31,777
Same kitchen, smarter choices.

33
00:01:32,427 --> 00:01:34,078
Data is just numbers.

34
00:01:34,078 --> 00:01:37,154
Information is numbers
that help you decide.

35
00:01:37,854 --> 00:01:40,513
Kotler splits the system into four parts.

36
00:01:40,863 --> 00:01:41,763
One.

37
00:01:41,384 --> 00:01:42,632
Internal records.

38
00:01:42,632 --> 00:01:47,285
What happens inside the business:
orders, sales, stock and payments.

39
00:01:47,635 --> 00:01:48,535
Two.

40
00:01:48,165 --> 00:01:49,745
Marketing intelligence.

41
00:01:49,745 --> 00:01:54,319
Everyday news from outside, about
customers, rivals and the market.

42
00:01:54,669 --> 00:01:55,569
Three.

43
00:01:55,298 --> 00:01:56,658
Marketing research.

44
00:01:56,658 --> 00:01:59,883
A special study that
answers one clear question.

45
00:02:00,233 --> 00:02:01,133
Four.

46
00:02:00,829 --> 00:02:02,127
Decision support.

47
00:02:02,127 --> 00:02:06,296
Tools and models that turn all
of this into a smart choice.

48
00:02:06,946 --> 00:02:09,769
So how is intelligence
different from research?

49
00:02:10,119 --> 00:02:12,853
Intelligence is always on, like a radar.

50
00:02:12,853 --> 00:02:15,291
It picks up small signals every day.

51
00:02:15,641 --> 00:02:18,964
Research is switched on for
one question, like a torch.

52
00:02:18,964 --> 00:02:21,038
When the answer comes, it stops.

53
00:02:21,688 --> 00:02:23,655
Where do we see this at work today?

54
00:02:24,005 --> 00:02:25,285
Internal records.

55
00:02:25,285 --> 00:02:29,271
A bakery's billing system shows
which bread sells out first.

56
00:02:29,621 --> 00:02:30,710
Intelligence.

57
00:02:30,710 --> 00:02:34,202
An airline checks rival
fares every single day.

58
00:02:34,552 --> 00:02:35,452
Research.

59
00:02:35,405 --> 00:02:39,902
A phone maker tests two designs
with real users before launch.

60
00:02:40,252 --> 00:02:41,466
Decision support.

61
00:02:41,466 --> 00:02:46,085
A food delivery app predicts how many
riders it needs on a rainy night.

62
00:02:46,735 --> 00:02:48,746
But is more data always better?

63
00:02:49,096 --> 00:02:50,181
The good side.

64
00:02:50,181 --> 00:02:53,078
Fewer guesses, less
waste and faster choices.

65
00:02:53,428 --> 00:02:54,620
The hard side.

66
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:59,282
Too much data confuses people, and
old data leads to wrong choices.

67
00:02:59,632 --> 00:03:03,276
Dev wants to post the customer
list in a big group chat.

68
00:03:03,276 --> 00:03:04,320
Zoya says no.

69
00:03:04,670 --> 00:03:06,208
Phone numbers are private.

70
00:03:06,208 --> 00:03:08,020
Only the team should see them.

71
00:03:08,370 --> 00:03:13,559
In India, the Digital Personal Data
Protection Act of 2023 allows fines

72
00:03:13,559 --> 00:03:18,947
up to two hundred and fifty crore
rupees for failing to keep personal data

73
00:03:18,947 --> 00:03:19,847
safe.

74
00:03:19,954 --> 00:03:20,854
The lesson?

75
00:03:20,791 --> 00:03:23,783
Collect what helps you
decide, and keep it safe.

76
00:03:24,433 --> 00:03:25,340
Quick check.

77
00:03:25,340 --> 00:03:28,566
Dev sees a new snack stall
opening near the college.

78
00:03:28,566 --> 00:03:30,736
Which part of the system is this?

79
00:03:32,636 --> 00:03:34,251
Marketing intelligence!

80
00:03:34,251 --> 00:03:38,077
It is everyday news about
the world outside Laddoo Lab.

81
00:03:38,677 --> 00:03:39,686
So, remember.

82
00:03:39,986 --> 00:03:44,283
A marketing information system gets
the right facts to the right people,

83
00:03:44,283 --> 00:03:45,619
in time to decide.

84
00:03:45,969 --> 00:03:50,313
It has four parts: internal records,
intelligence, research and decision

85
00:03:50,313 --> 00:03:51,213
support.

86
00:03:51,341 --> 00:03:53,309
Intelligence is always on.

87
00:03:53,309 --> 00:03:55,497
Research answers one question.

88
00:03:56,097 --> 00:03:59,551
Next time, we'll explore
marketing research fundamentals.
